Who else would I mean?

279
00:10:38,140 --> 00:10:40,160
That came out of left field, so I wasn't sure.

280
00:10:40,880 --> 00:10:42,780
But yeah, it's a mystery.

281
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:43,840
Hmm.

282
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:46,940
A mystery you've already solved, perhaps.

283
00:10:47,300 --> 00:10:47,940
Negatory.

284
00:10:50,780 --> 00:10:51,540
It's cold.

285
00:10:52,020 --> 00:10:53,700
Hey, Prez. Let me warm up in here.

286
00:10:54,540 --> 00:10:54,880
Oh.

287
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:57,160
What's going on, Ishikawa?

288
00:10:57,720 --> 00:10:58,200
Sup.

289
00:10:58,600 --> 00:11:00,920
Like a Miyamura moth to the flame, here you are.

290
00:11:01,060 --> 00:11:02,320
What? There's no fire.

291
00:11:02,860 --> 00:11:04,140
Come right on in!

292
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:06,100
You're a little too happy to see me.

293
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:07,320
Miyamura?

294
00:11:08,260 --> 00:11:09,300
Aren't you hot?

295
00:11:10,100 --> 00:11:12,080
I told you I came because I'm cold.

296
00:11:12,580 --> 00:11:13,860
You'll heat up pretty quick, though.

297
00:11:14,260 --> 00:11:15,960
See how Ishikawa dished his blazer?

298
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:17,540
That's how toasty he is.

299
00:11:17,660 --> 00:11:18,100
Dude.

300
00:11:18,420 --> 00:11:19,680
How obvious can you be?

301
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:21,040
He got that warm?

302
00:11:22,040 --> 00:11:23,800
Maybe I'll ditch it a little later.

303
00:11:24,880 --> 00:11:25,380
Blast.

304
00:11:25,940 --> 00:11:28,420
Have I ever seen you in a school sweater before?

305
00:11:28,660 --> 00:11:29,520
I don't own one.

306
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:31,900
It'd look nice.

307
00:11:32,220 --> 00:11:33,580
Snug in all the red spots.

308
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:36,500
Hey, why don't you try mine on it, see if you like how it fits you?

309
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:37,500
You're scaring me.

310
00:11:38,920 --> 00:11:39,320
Here.

311
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:41,800
Oh, feels legit.

312
00:11:43,660 --> 00:11:45,260
My plan actually worked.

313
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:48,740
At last, he'll change his clothes and I'll see what he's been hiding.

314
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:52,200
Miyamura said his tattoos show through a white button down.

315
00:11:52,760 --> 00:11:55,960
He's totally cut onto Sengoku's scheme and is just gonna...

316
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:56,660
He's gotta be kidding!

317
00:11:57,380 --> 00:11:57,820
Yes!

318
00:11:58,060 --> 00:11:59,020
Take off your sweater!

319
00:11:59,780 --> 00:12:01,240
No, he's gonna find out!

320
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:07,980
Are you all right?

321
00:12:12,980 --> 00:12:14,200
It's so warm.

322
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:17,060
And the material for these things is top notch.

323
00:12:17,420 --> 00:12:18,120
How do I look, huh?

324
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:18,700
Tell me.

325
00:12:18,940 --> 00:12:20,040
You look great!

326
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:24,520
I really thought today would be the day.

327
00:12:25,240 --> 00:12:25,840
What day?

328
00:12:26,300 --> 00:12:28,280
I'm just gonna come right out and ask.

329
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:30,700
Why are you so against removing your clothes?

330
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:32,480
Because I'm rational.

331
00:12:32,840 --> 00:12:35,060
I'm not suggesting you prance around Stark naked.

332
00:12:35,420 --> 00:12:37,520
I meant when you changed for P.E. and stuff.

333
00:12:38,220 --> 00:12:39,000
What's this?

334
00:12:39,200 --> 00:12:41,160
Is the president obsessed with me?

335
00:12:41,160 --> 00:12:41,700
As if!

336
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:43,560
I just really, really want to know!

337
00:12:43,740 --> 00:12:44,380
Why's that?

338
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:46,240
It has to go without saying, shouldn't it?

339
00:12:46,780 --> 00:12:48,680
Because it's clearly not normal behavior!

340
00:12:48,680 --> 00:12:50,140
And why's that?

341
00:12:50,220 --> 00:12:51,240
Calm down, Miyamura!

342
00:12:52,700 --> 00:12:54,700
The God President's bullying me!

343
00:12:54,700 --> 00:12:55,040
Ah!

344
00:12:55,180 --> 00:12:56,300
I stole my sweater!

345
00:12:56,580 --> 00:12:57,520
Give it back!

346
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:02,600
That's a school sweater you have on right now.

347
00:13:06,180 --> 00:13:07,840
Why'd you sprint here, dummy?

348
00:13:08,460 --> 00:13:10,160
Oh, welcome home, son.

349
00:13:10,460 --> 00:13:12,200
Is that a new sweater you're wearing?

350
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:14,160
He got away.

351
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:22,760
Let's go.

352
00:13:23,500 --> 00:13:24,780
Before we turn into ice.

353
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:28,700
Hey, thanks for waiting.

354
00:13:30,700 --> 00:13:31,180
Hmm?

355
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:33,460
Shall we?

356
00:13:33,820 --> 00:13:34,160
Yeah.

357
00:13:39,880 --> 00:13:40,880
It's freezing.

358
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:42,780
This recent snow made me realize

359
00:13:42,780 --> 00:13:44,280
spring is still far away.

360
00:13:45,020 --> 00:13:46,580
I'm sorry you have to wear a skirt.

361
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:48,280
So cold.

362
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:53,020
Hands.

363
00:13:53,460 --> 00:13:53,940
Hands.

364
00:13:54,620 --> 00:13:54,860
Huh?

365
00:13:56,300 --> 00:13:56,740
Here.

366
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:01,680
Yes, Remy.

367
00:14:02,220 --> 00:14:03,600
You're very cold.

368
00:14:04,080 --> 00:14:04,560
Nuh-oh.

369
00:14:04,700 --> 00:14:05,380
Remy's warm.

370
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:07,220
But I'm cold.

371
00:14:07,220 --> 00:14:08,680
You took the cold for me

372
00:14:08,680 --> 00:14:10,200
and now I'm warm as I can be.

373
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:11,980
Is that a fact?

374
00:14:13,160 --> 00:14:13,720
Hand.

375
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:15,280
Yeah, yeah.

376
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:20,140
Hmm.

377
00:14:30,140 --> 00:14:30,940
Hmm?

378
00:14:32,020 --> 00:14:33,560
Hold my hand, silly!

379
00:14:34,100 --> 00:14:35,180
She's angry?

380
00:14:35,180 --> 00:14:43,020
Walk properly, please.

381
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:48,340
She feels warm.

382
00:14:50,320 --> 00:14:52,180
Sengoku, you warming up?

383
00:14:52,800 --> 00:14:53,180
Mm-hmm.

384
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:55,340
Then I guess that only makes one of us.

385
00:14:55,680 --> 00:14:57,340
Remy's hand is still ice cold,

386
00:14:57,580 --> 00:14:59,680
but yours are bony enough to be a skeleton's.

387
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:00,260
Oh.

388
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,280
You want to let go?

389
00:15:02,880 --> 00:15:03,760
Not at all.

390
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:05,740
Remy's hands aren't perfect either.

391
00:15:05,980 --> 00:15:06,580
They're tiny.

392
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:08,020
They're fine.

393
00:15:09,220 --> 00:15:12,300
Do you feel like going somewhere, or...?

394
00:15:12,300 --> 00:15:13,980
Nah.

395
00:15:19,220 --> 00:15:20,980
You picked up the pace.

396
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:22,940
Because I wasn't paying attention.

397
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:25,060
Then pay attention.

398
00:15:25,520 --> 00:15:25,900
Right.

399
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:28,960
Remy wants to walk slower.

400
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:31,800
Any slower and we would...

401
00:15:31,800 --> 00:15:31,960
Ugh!

402
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:33,120
Stop.

403
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:36,120
You're almost home.

404
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:37,500
Went from freezing cold

405
00:15:37,500 --> 00:15:39,020
to just freezing in place.

406
00:15:39,380 --> 00:15:40,220
What's going on?

407
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:45,640
Hug.

408
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:46,140
Uh...

409
00:15:46,140 --> 00:15:54,560
Never mind.

410
00:15:58,340 --> 00:15:58,900
Hug?

411
00:16:04,020 --> 00:16:04,500
Okay.

412
00:16:08,020 --> 00:16:08,500
Yay!

413
00:16:08,700 --> 00:16:09,100
Hug!

414
00:16:09,100 --> 00:16:15,680
Let me have my arms back for a minute, Remy.

415
00:16:21,060 --> 00:16:21,840
Much better.

416
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:28,800
Kiss.

417
00:16:29,580 --> 00:16:29,920
No.

418
00:16:30,440 --> 00:16:31,300
We're on the street.

419
00:16:31,300 --> 00:16:33,300
I understand.

420
00:16:33,300 --> 00:16:34,180
I understand.

421
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:35,260
Good.

422
00:16:40,220 --> 00:16:41,620
Hey, we better get going.

423
00:16:42,340 --> 00:16:44,060
The library's gonna close in five.

424
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:44,640
Oh!

425
00:16:45,200 --> 00:16:45,920
You're right!

426
00:16:46,260 --> 00:16:47,120
Oh, man.

427
00:16:47,860 --> 00:16:49,980
Remy's head feels like it's gonna explode.

428
00:16:50,420 --> 00:16:51,820
You did use it a lot today.

429
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:54,540
And you're sure you don't want me to go over your math homework?

430
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:55,400
Positive.

431
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:57,300
I can do that assignment by myself.

432
00:16:58,240 --> 00:16:58,760
Think so?

433
00:16:59,240 --> 00:16:59,540
Yep!

434
00:16:59,540 --> 00:17:02,320
Let's go, Sakura!

435
00:17:09,100 --> 00:17:09,620
Sengoku.

436
00:17:10,580 --> 00:17:12,100
Would you like to walk home together?

437
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:15,720
Sure.

438
00:17:16,180 --> 00:17:16,700
Got everything?

439
00:17:17,140 --> 00:17:18,020
Yeah, I'm good.

440
00:17:20,960 --> 00:17:22,620
You look ready for a blizzard.

441
00:17:22,980 --> 00:17:24,180
Because I'm cold-hearted.

442
00:17:24,380 --> 00:17:25,480
I didn't say that.

443
00:17:26,820 --> 00:17:28,200
Hori, what you looking at?

444
00:17:28,860 --> 00:17:29,000
Huh?

445
00:17:29,540 --> 00:17:30,240
Where's Remy?

446
00:17:30,720 --> 00:17:31,180
Dunno.

447
00:17:31,700 --> 00:17:34,080
It's pretty unusual to see those two by themselves.

448
00:17:34,860 --> 00:17:37,200
Yeah, I was thinking the same thing.

449
00:17:37,880 --> 00:17:38,280
Hmm...

450
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:39,000
Hmm...

451
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:41,860
Well, whatever.

452
00:17:41,860 --> 00:17:45,060
It's not like I spend every waking second with my boyfriend.

453
00:17:45,220 --> 00:17:46,200
Yeah, exactly!

454
00:17:47,160 --> 00:17:47,660
Hey!

455
00:17:47,880 --> 00:17:49,380
Real quick question for you ladies!

456
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:51,640
Have you seen Sengoku or Sakura?

457
00:17:52,200 --> 00:17:52,440
Huh?

458
00:17:53,100 --> 00:17:57,520
They were here a minute ago, but then Remy went to the bathroom, and now they're gone!

459
00:17:57,520 --> 00:18:00,060
Are you ready for a storm?

460
00:18:00,060 --> 00:18:01,260
You ready for a storm?

461
00:18:01,260 --> 00:18:02,560
The one in my heart.

462
00:18:02,560 --> 00:18:05,180
Well, here and last, I guess!

463
00:18:05,180 --> 00:18:07,680
Oh, what was that for?

464
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:09,020
Take a guess!

465
00:18:09,680 --> 00:18:10,400
It's fine!

466
00:18:10,400 --> 00:18:11,400
It's fine!

467
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:12,300
It's fine!

468
00:18:12,300 --> 00:18:12,700
It is!

469
00:18:12,780 --> 00:18:13,360
But hush!

470
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:16,940
And what if it was like that, but it's not?

471
00:18:17,060 --> 00:18:17,600
Like what?

472
00:18:18,220 --> 00:18:19,940
You weren't hiding something, right?

473
00:18:20,440 --> 00:18:20,680
No.

474
00:18:20,800 --> 00:18:21,760
What would we have to hide?

475
00:18:22,300 --> 00:18:22,780
Hori?

476
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:25,780
They could have stopped in the student council room.

477
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:27,520
I'll try giving them a call.

478
00:18:28,180 --> 00:18:28,540
Ah!

479
00:18:28,540 --> 00:18:30,200
I'm okay!

480
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:33,160
Do you see that over on the window straight across from us?

481
00:18:33,340 --> 00:18:36,020
There's a giant, really weird-looking bug just chilling out!

482
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:37,580
I want to see the giant bug!

483
00:18:37,720 --> 00:18:37,920
Look!

484
00:18:38,340 --> 00:18:41,740
Leave it to Hori to worry about a problem that doesn't exist.

485
00:18:42,520 --> 00:18:43,200
Hey, boss!

486
00:18:43,800 --> 00:18:44,900
Is the S&C 60?

487
00:18:44,900 --> 00:18:45,340
You're okay?

488
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:46,000
Sure.

489
00:18:52,920 --> 00:18:54,780
How much trash did you throw away?

490
00:18:55,400 --> 00:18:56,900
Got distracted by the president.

491
00:18:57,200 --> 00:18:57,860
He's here with Kono.

492
00:18:57,860 --> 00:18:58,760
Hmm.

493
00:18:59,840 --> 00:19:02,240
What caught me off guard is Ayasaki's M.I.A.

494
00:19:02,780 --> 00:19:05,660
And the bag that Kono had with her looked like it might be a gift.

495
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:06,840
Dude!

496
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:07,940
You spilled everywhere!

497
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:09,480
Then he's cheating!

498
00:19:09,700 --> 00:19:10,600
Don't jump to conclusions!

499
00:19:11,580 --> 00:19:11,820
Oh!

500
00:19:12,740 --> 00:19:14,360
Ayasaki's on the market again now!

501
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:15,540
It's my chance.

502
00:19:15,800 --> 00:19:17,380
I repeat, don't jump to conclusions.

503
00:19:17,740 --> 00:19:19,320
And why am I the one cleaning your mess?

504
00:19:19,560 --> 00:19:20,280
You do it!

505
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,080
You would, uh, yep.

506
00:19:22,300 --> 00:19:23,400
Knew that loud voice was yours.

507
00:19:23,420 --> 00:19:23,740
Ah!

508
00:19:24,560 --> 00:19:26,340
I wasn't having shady thoughts!

509
00:19:26,600 --> 00:19:27,000
Huh?

510
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:30,500
Noticed her sans Ayasaki for today, huh?

511
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:32,460
Yes, for today.

512
00:19:33,120 --> 00:19:35,600
I'm not sure how to interpret that response.

513
00:19:36,520 --> 00:19:37,820
Don't tell her that I was here.

514
00:19:38,040 --> 00:19:38,560
Oh-ho!

515
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:40,640
What exactly will happen if I do?

516
00:19:40,700 --> 00:19:41,580
Shut the hell up!

517
00:19:42,060 --> 00:19:42,320
Huh?

518
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:45,240
Do not tell her I was here.

519
00:19:45,280 --> 00:19:46,520
I'll take it to the grave.

520
00:19:46,520 --> 00:19:49,320
What was that?

521
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:51,180
See you later.

522
00:19:51,580 --> 00:19:51,940
Bye.

523
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:53,100
Till tomorrow.

524
00:19:53,100 --> 00:20:02,900
Please don't ask the impossible of me, Sakura!

525
00:20:03,620 --> 00:20:07,800
I've never scored above a 40 in math ever, so it's no go!

526
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:09,660
Just 60 points!

527
00:20:09,780 --> 00:20:10,180
No!

528
00:20:10,180 --> 00:20:15,640
Hmm, score at least 60, and we'll visit that chocolate shop you like.

529
00:20:15,640 --> 00:20:16,640
We can get...

530
00:20:16,640 --> 00:20:17,500
The premium cookies?

531
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:19,680
Mm-hmm, yeah, those ones.

532
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:22,120
Oh, neat to try.

533
00:20:22,240 --> 00:20:24,520
But Remy isn't motivated by material things.

534
00:20:24,880 --> 00:20:26,320
Well, good luck anyway.

535
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:32,320
Right, next tier we have...

536
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:33,120
Nice job.

537
00:20:33,620 --> 00:20:36,040
You finally scored higher than a 40 on a test.

538
00:20:36,040 --> 00:20:42,140
Remy said that she isn't motivated by material things.

539
00:20:42,580 --> 00:20:42,960
Huh?

540
00:20:44,920 --> 00:20:45,480
Hmm.

541
00:20:55,920 --> 00:20:56,840
Good morning.

542
00:20:58,680 --> 00:20:59,240
Sakura!

543
00:20:59,720 --> 00:21:01,580
Why did you leave without me yesterday?

544
00:21:02,040 --> 00:21:03,040
Where did you go?

545
00:21:03,500 --> 00:21:04,460
Sorry about that.

546
00:21:04,460 --> 00:21:06,120
I was getting a little...

547
00:21:06,120 --> 00:21:06,820
Sweet treat.

548
00:21:07,740 --> 00:21:08,620
The cookies!

549
00:21:09,180 --> 00:21:12,360
How come Remy got less than a 60 on the milk exam?

550
00:21:12,440 --> 00:21:13,780
Which is irrelevant.

551
00:21:15,040 --> 00:21:17,700
I was just in that area and decided to treat myself.

552
00:21:22,740 --> 00:21:23,920
Wow, you were right.

553
00:21:24,220 --> 00:21:24,980
These are good.

554
00:21:25,620 --> 00:21:26,560
Wait a second.

555
00:21:26,780 --> 00:21:28,120
Remy wants them too, please.

556
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:29,280
Go right ahead.

557
00:21:29,280 --> 00:21:36,180
I bake my own cookies every once in a while, but it's hard to pass up a nice shop like that.

558
00:21:40,060 --> 00:21:40,780
Thanks, Sakura.

559
00:21:41,280 --> 00:21:42,100
You're awesome.

560
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:42,940
Hmm?

561
00:21:43,680 --> 00:21:44,560
You say something?

562
00:21:46,060 --> 00:21:46,760
Sure, Dennis!

563
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:48,240
Oh, okay.

564
00:21:48,720 --> 00:21:48,940
Oh!

565
00:21:49,320 --> 00:21:51,220
We should save some cookies for Sengoku.

566
00:21:51,500 --> 00:21:52,420
No, we shouldn't.

567
00:21:52,820 --> 00:21:55,420
Remy would have that much less if I ate any cookies.

568
00:21:55,420 --> 00:21:57,420
I'm sorry.

